[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two shallow, matte ceramic bowls set on an aged, dark oak wood tabletop, centered in the frame with generous negative space. The camera is at a 3/4 overhead angle (40°), ensuring the full interior of both bowls is visible and well-defined. Soft, natural side light from a window on the left creates a gentle sheen on the broth and soft shadows. The soup is a hearty, rustic combination of lean, golden-browned ground chicken crumbles, vibrant dark red kidney beans, tender whole wheat rotini, soft diced tomatoes, and dark green ribbons of wilted spinach submerged in a clear, golden-hued chicken broth. The ingredients are evenly distributed, not layered, showing texture and individual components. Beside the bowls, a worn wooden spoon rests casually on the table, with a few stray spinach leaves and a faint drop of broth near the edge of the wood. The background is softly blurred, showing a linen napkin. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating—lived-in, warm, authentic. Slight natural imperfections: a small broth drip on the rim of the bowl, uneven browning on the chicken pieces. NO carrots, NO celery, NO unlisted vegetables, no plastic sheen, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from professional editorial food photography for a cookbook."
]
